 61ZN    28SI(36AR,2PNG)               2009AN01                  15NDS    201503
 61ZN  H TYP=FUL$AUT=KAZIMIERZ ZUBER, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 125, 1 (2015)$       
 61ZN2 H CUT=25-Jan-2015$                                                       
 61ZN c  2009An01: E=142, 148 MeV beam provided by ATLAS-ANL facility.          
 61ZN2c  Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, (particle)|g coin, angular distributions      
 61ZN3c  using GAMMASPHERE array of Ge detectors. The charged particles were    
 61ZN4c  detected using Microball array and |DE-E telescopes. Comparisons with  
 61ZN5c  cranked Nilsson-Strutinsky calculations. See also 2006An31 from        
 61ZN6c  the same group using {+40}Ca({+24}Mg,2pn|g) reaction. See also dataset 
 61ZN7c  for this reaction                                                      
 61ZN c  1999Yu10: E=143 MeV; also {+40}Ca({+29}Si,2|a|g)                       
 61ZN2c  E=130 MeV. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, particle-|g coin, |g|g(|q)(DCO)    
 61ZN3c  using GAMMASPHERE array of 82 and 100 Compton-suppressed Ge            
 61ZN4c  detectors and 95-element CsI Microball. Deduced SD-1 band and          
 61ZN5c  interconnecting transitions of 5172 and 5278 keV to normal band.       
 61ZN6c  Interband transition of 5278 keV is confirmed in 2009An01.             
 61ZN c  Level scheme below 8500-keV level shown in figure 1 of 2009An01        
 61ZN2c  is taken from their previous work reported in 2006An31, which used     
 61ZN3c  {+40}Ca({+24}Mg,2pn|g) reaction.                                       
 61ZN cG E$From 2006An31 for transitions from levels up to 8500 keV, all others 
 61ZN2cG are from 2009An01                                                      
 61ZN cG M$From |g|g(|q) data. The |DJ=2, quadrupole transitions, multipolarity 
 61ZN2cG is most likely E2, and for interband transitions, |DJ=1,0, D+Q is most 
 61ZN3cG likely M1+E2.                                                          
 61ZN DG $ E(A),RI(A): From 61MN B-Decay (623 NS) (1985Ru05).                   
 61ZN cG $R(30|'-83|') is angular asymmetry ratio: expected ratio is |?1.6-1.7  
 61ZN2cG for |DJ=2, quadrupole and |?0.7-0.8 for |DJ=1, dipole transition       
 61ZN cL $Nomenclature for configuration assignments is                         
 61ZN2cL [p{-1}p{-2},n{-1}n{-2}], where p{-1} and n{-1} denote number of proton 
 61ZN3cL or neutron holes in the orbitals of high-j 1f{-7/2} shell; p{-2} and   
 61ZN4cL n{-2} denote the number of (proton or neutron) particles in the        
 61ZN5cL high-j 1g{-9/2} shell, relative to the closed {+56}Ni core. Active     
 61ZN6cL orbitals for protons and neutrons are: 1f{-7/2}, 1g{-9/2}, 1f{-5/2},   
 61ZN7cL 2p{-3/2} and 2p{-1/2}; the number of particles in the last three       
 61ZN8cL orbitals are denoted as p{-3} or n{-3}                                 
 61ZN cL E$From least-squares fit to E|g data.                                  
 61ZN cL J$ As proposed in 2009An01 and 2006An31 based on |g|g(|q) data         
 61ZN2cL for selected transitions and band associations. See also Adopted       
 61ZN3cL Levels for recommended values                                          
